---
import Arduino from '~icons/simple-icons/arduino'
import Claude from '~icons/simple-icons/claude'
import Eslint from '~icons/simple-icons/eslint'
import Forgejo from '~icons/simple-icons/forgejo'
import Gamepad from '~icons/tabler/device-gamepad-2'
import Github from '~icons/simple-icons/github'
import Godot from '~icons/simple-icons/godotengine'
import Mail from '~icons/tabler/mail'
import Mcp from '~icons/simple-icons/modelcontextprotocol'
import Nuxt from '~icons/simple-icons/nuxt'
import Php from '~icons/simple-icons/php'
import Processing from '~icons/simple-icons/processingfoundation'
import Symfony from '~icons/simple-icons/symfony'
import IconLink from '../components/icon-link.kay'
---
head
  title About
  meta(name="description" content="Kévyn, a full-stack developer from Bordeaux: how I got into coding, and what I care about in it.")
article.mx-auto.max-w-2xl
  h1.mb-10.text-3xl.font-semibold About
  .prose
    p I'm Kévyn, a full-stack developer from Bordeaux, France. I build web apps for a living, and Minecraft mods, tools and #[IconLink(href="https://godotengine.org" icon={Godot}) Godot] projects for fun.
    h2 How I got here
    p It started with an #[IconLink(href="https://www.arduino.cc" icon={Arduino}) Arduino], discovered at a family meal when I was twelve. I spent a year playing with it, then drifted to the screen: some very basic HTML, a lot of #[IconLink(href="https://processing.org" icon={Processing}) Processing], and Discord bots hosted on Glitch. A friend saw one of those bots and asked me for a custom one, then bought me a VPS, my first real server: it taught me a lot about Linux and how to host things on the internet.
    p Processing came back in seconde, my first year of high school, when a class asked us to use it. I handed in a platform game, and the teacher had a hard time believing I had made it myself, though one look at the code would have settled it: it was a mess that would burn my eyes today. Around the same time, I wrote a Discord bot for a YouTuber, who paid for another VPS so I could run it there.
    p All of that made a real difference once I got to my computer science IUT, where, I admit, I spent more classes than I should have playing #[IconLink(href="https://www.dofus.com" icon={Gamepad}) Dofus], and even more playing video games once Covid moved classes online and nobody could see my screen. A one-year work-study web degree followed (licence pro en alternance), and right after it, the job I've now held for four years. There, I build large #[IconLink(href="https://nuxt.com" icon={Nuxt}) Nuxt] and #[IconLink(href="https://symfony.com" icon={Symfony}) Symfony] projects over several months, then maintain them, migrating to new versions to keep them secure.
    p I also still host my own things, on my own server running #[IconLink(href="https://forgejo.org" icon={Forgejo}) Forgejo], this blog and a few personal tools. My data stays mine, it costs little, the footprint stays small, and I keep learning from it, which is half the fun.
    h2 What I care about
    p Developer experience, performance and accessibility, and the footprint of what I build: the smaller it is, the less it costs, both to the people using it and to the planet, which never asked for a 2 MB JavaScript bundle.
    p I'm also picky about code itself, and about formatting most of all: code should breathe. I started #[IconLink(href="https://github.com/Kayno0o/eslint" icon={Eslint}) my own ESLint ruleset] as a layer over #[IconLink(href="https://github.com/antfu/eslint-config" icon={Github}) antfu's], and ended up rewriting it from scratch. At work, I set up a very strict #[IconLink(href="https://cs.symfony.com" icon={Php}) PHP CS Fixer] config, half to annoy my coworkers, half so I stop grumbling when I read their code.
    h2 What I use
    p I code with #[IconLink(href="https://claude.com/product/claude-code" icon={Claude}) Claude Code], extended with my own memory server (an #[IconLink(href="https://modelcontextprotocol.io" icon={Mcp}) MCP] server), hooks and mods, so it remembers how I like my code to breathe. The rest of my setup:
    ul
      li I use Arch, btw (and Manjaro)
      li KDE Plasma on Wayland
      li fish, in kitty with tmux
      li Brave
    h2 Get in touch
    p Contributions to kay are welcome, and so are questions: open an issue on #[IconLink(href="https://github.com/Kayno0o/kayjs" icon={Github}) kay's repository], or write to me at #[IconLink(href="mailto:contact@kaynooo.fr" icon={Mail}) contact@kaynooo.fr].
